WEBVTT

00:01.710 --> 00:04.171
[theme music playing]

00:22.981 --> 00:24.858
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:33.552 --> 01:35.387
Finding a way back up was rough,

01:35.470 --> 01:37.472
so of course, when we try to go back down,

01:37.556 --> 01:39.683
we run into something like this.

01:39.766 --> 01:42.227
[Chilchuck breathes deeply]
I don't like it at all.

01:42.310 --> 01:44.104
This blood hasn't dried yet.

01:44.187 --> 01:47.858
Falin must have passed through recently
to head to the lower floors.

01:49.109 --> 01:50.861
I bet she was cramped in here.

01:51.570 --> 01:53.238
[narrator] <i>The sixth floor.</i>

01:53.321 --> 01:55.824
<i>Underground waterways that utilize tunnels</i>

01:55.907 --> 01:57.492
<i>dug by ancient dwarves.</i>

01:57.576 --> 01:59.828
<i>They appear to stretch out endlessly,</i>

01:59.911 --> 02:03.748
<i>laying themselves under the town
like the roots of a tree.</i>

02:03.832 --> 02:07.586
<i>Besides the water,
many things likely flowed through here.</i>

02:07.669 --> 02:09.963
<i>Humans and animals,</i>

02:10.046 --> 02:12.632
<i>conspiracies, and rumors.</i>

02:13.216 --> 02:15.510
<i>Money and blood.</i>

02:16.094 --> 02:17.429
[Marcille] It's so cold.

02:17.512 --> 02:18.889
[Laios]
Yeah, it's weird since I'm pretty sure

02:18.972 --> 02:20.724
this floor is supposed to be humid.

02:20.807 --> 02:21.725
[Laios exhales softly]

02:21.808 --> 02:23.518
[Marcille]
Maybe we ended up somewhere else?

02:23.602 --> 02:26.271
I think I remember this route from before.

02:26.354 --> 02:28.106
[Chilchuck]
<i>Yeah, this is definitely the floor</i>

02:28.190 --> 02:29.941
<i>where the Red Dragon attacked us</i>

02:30.025 --> 02:31.776
<i>and almost wiped out our party.</i>

02:31.860 --> 02:34.905
I mean, it is a dungeon
where walls and roads move around.

02:34.988 --> 02:37.282
The temperature changing
isn't that strange.

02:37.365 --> 02:40.202
[Laios]
I prefer it being cold over it being hot.

02:40.285 --> 02:43.788
But the snow and water washing away
the bloodstains is a big problem.

02:43.872 --> 02:46.207
[Chilchuck] Since we're here,
do we wanna head back to the place

02:46.291 --> 02:47.584
where we almost got wiped?

02:47.667 --> 02:49.794
If the Dungeon Cleaners
haven't gotten to it yet,

02:49.878 --> 02:51.796
we might be able to salvage our stuff.

02:51.880 --> 02:54.049
I wonder if Falin is doing okay.

02:54.132 --> 02:56.968
I'd imagine this cold is pretty tough
on Red Dragons.

02:57.052 --> 02:59.054
Wait, is that why she had feathers?

02:59.137 --> 03:01.723
So, Laios, since you got in Shuro's face

03:01.806 --> 03:04.392
and blurted out
we were gonna defeat the mad mage,

03:04.476 --> 03:06.561
surely you must have
some kind of plan, right?

03:07.228 --> 03:08.438
Yeah, about that…

03:09.064 --> 03:12.359
[Laios] <i>Falin said she was looking
for someone named Delgal.</i>

03:12.442 --> 03:15.862
<i>I imagine the mad mage had given
the Red Dragon that same order.</i>

03:16.655 --> 03:19.741
<i>That's also the reason the Red Dragon
came up to a different floor</i>

03:19.824 --> 03:21.785
<i>and wandered around without resting.</i>

03:22.702 --> 03:23.912
[Senshi] Who's Delgal?

03:23.995 --> 03:26.957
[Chilchuck] The name sounds familiar,
but I'm drawing a blank.

03:27.040 --> 03:28.041
[Marcille] It's the king.

03:28.124 --> 03:29.000
[both] Hmm?

03:29.584 --> 03:32.462
When the Golden Country fell
1,000 years ago,

03:32.545 --> 03:34.047
he was their last ruler.

03:34.589 --> 03:37.467
[Marcille] <i>You can find engravings
in various spots of this dungeon</i>

03:37.550 --> 03:38.677
<i>that sing his praises.</i>

03:38.760 --> 03:39.886
[Chilchuck] <i>Oh, that's right!</i>

03:39.970 --> 03:42.013
<i>His name is on artifacts
that have been dug up.</i>

03:42.097 --> 03:43.223
Hang on.

03:43.306 --> 03:44.933
But didn't I hear that he…

03:45.016 --> 03:46.017
Yeah.

03:46.101 --> 03:48.144
[Laios] <i>When this dungeon
was initially discovered,</i>

03:48.228 --> 03:52.023
<i>he briefly appeared on the surface,
became dust, and vanished.</i>

03:52.107 --> 03:53.900
[Chilchuck]
So, the mad mage has been working

03:53.984 --> 03:55.068
the Red Dragon to the bone

03:55.151 --> 03:57.612
and completely changing
the dungeon's structure,

03:57.696 --> 04:00.073
all to find a king
who disappeared ages ago?

04:00.156 --> 04:03.076
[Laios] Ever since the mad mage witnessed
the previous king get killed

04:03.159 --> 04:04.327
right in front of him,

04:04.411 --> 04:07.163
he's worried
that his son will meet the same fate.

04:07.247 --> 04:09.624
That's why he must have assumed
we were assassins

04:09.708 --> 04:11.626
-and started attacking us.
-[sneezes]

04:11.710 --> 04:13.962
Really? Where'd you hear that from?

04:14.045 --> 04:15.046
A dream?

04:15.130 --> 04:17.299
Oh, uh… Well, you see…

04:17.382 --> 04:20.635
[Laios] <i>I first met the mad mage
inside of the Living Paintings.</i>

04:20.719 --> 04:22.554
<i>And that's where I learned about it.</i>

04:22.637 --> 04:25.307
[Laios] Remember… I told you
that I tried to eat some food in there

04:25.390 --> 04:27.559
and he was so pissed at me?

04:27.642 --> 04:28.476
-[Marcille] What?
-[groans]

04:28.560 --> 04:29.769
[Chilchuck]
Why didn't you mention that sooner?

04:29.853 --> 04:32.314
I only put the pieces together just now!

04:32.981 --> 04:33.982
Huh, I see.

04:34.065 --> 04:36.318
So you are reliving the past.

04:36.401 --> 04:37.902
[Chilchuck] To be absolutely sure,

04:37.986 --> 04:40.238
you said that the mad mage
was an elf, right?

04:40.322 --> 04:42.657
Do elves really live up to 1,000 years?

04:42.741 --> 04:44.909
[Marcille]
There were records of it a long time ago,

04:44.993 --> 04:48.330
but currently,
our typical lifespan is about 500 at best.

04:48.413 --> 04:49.998
[Chilchuck] At best, huh?

04:50.081 --> 04:52.751
Well, I mean, you're able to mess
with other people's lives,

04:52.834 --> 04:56.087
so I'd imagine it simple enough
for you to extend your own.

04:56.171 --> 04:57.547
That's not true!

04:57.630 --> 05:00.091
It's impossible to prolong your life
with your own magic.

05:00.175 --> 05:03.094
That'll be like someone trying
to eat their own flesh to live longer.

05:03.178 --> 05:05.680
Anyway, if he attacked us
because he thought

05:05.764 --> 05:07.098
that we were enemies of the king…

05:07.182 --> 05:09.184
maybe we can clear things up with him?

05:09.267 --> 05:10.435
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

05:11.061 --> 05:12.479
[worried groan]

05:12.562 --> 05:15.231
[wind gusting heavily]

05:15.315 --> 05:17.359
-[Marcille quivering]
-The wind's gotten way stronger.

05:17.442 --> 05:18.860
Why is it so cold?

05:18.943 --> 05:20.570
[Laios] <i>I can't see ahead.</i>

05:20.653 --> 05:21.738
Hey, you guys!

05:21.821 --> 05:23.114
Are you still following me?

05:23.198 --> 05:24.616
[Chilchuck] Laios, where did you go?

05:24.699 --> 05:26.242
[Senshi] I can't see anything!

05:26.326 --> 05:28.620
[Laios] It'd be bad if we got separated!

05:28.703 --> 05:30.288
Grab on to someone's hand!

05:30.372 --> 05:32.082
[quivering]

05:32.165 --> 05:34.084
[Senshi grunts, quivers]

05:35.001 --> 05:37.712
[quivering]

05:40.590 --> 05:42.342
[Laios] <i>We can't go on like this.</i>

05:44.219 --> 05:45.261
[Laios] A tunnel!

05:45.345 --> 05:47.263
Let's take shelter!

05:50.600 --> 05:52.268
[Laios panting]

05:55.855 --> 05:57.148
You guys okay?

05:57.232 --> 05:58.149
Chil?

05:58.233 --> 05:59.150
[Chilchuck] I'm here.

05:59.234 --> 06:00.235
No issues.

06:00.777 --> 06:01.653
Marcille?

06:01.736 --> 06:02.779
[Marcille] Present.

06:02.862 --> 06:04.155
I'm over here.

06:04.239 --> 06:05.156
Senshi?

06:05.240 --> 06:06.074
[Senshi] Yeah.

06:06.157 --> 06:06.991
All good.

06:07.075 --> 06:08.451
Oh, thank goodness.

06:08.535 --> 06:09.369
[Senshi] Hmm?

06:09.452 --> 06:10.578
-Hey, Marcille.
-[Chilchuck] Wait a sec…

06:10.662 --> 06:12.372
Could you give us some light, please?

06:12.455 --> 06:13.373
[chiming]

06:16.376 --> 06:18.294
[soft groan]

06:19.003 --> 06:20.338
[Laios] This place…

06:20.421 --> 06:22.298
It kinda looks like an old prison.

06:23.049 --> 06:25.385
For a while there, I thought we…

06:27.137 --> 06:28.304
[all] Huh?

06:28.388 --> 06:29.556
[all] No way!

06:29.639 --> 06:30.807
[all] Huh?

06:31.516 --> 06:32.559
[all] This is…

06:33.309 --> 06:35.562
-[Laios] <i>We've multiplied!</i>
-[unsettling music playing]

06:35.645 --> 06:37.689
Hey, the hell is all this?

06:37.772 --> 06:39.315
Illusion magic?

06:39.899 --> 06:40.942
Let's see.

06:41.025 --> 06:42.819
Hmm…

06:43.403 --> 06:46.322
My guess is…
it's the work of a Shapeshifter.

06:46.406 --> 06:47.574
Shape-what?

06:47.657 --> 06:48.783
[Laios] Never heard of them?

06:48.867 --> 06:51.703
Where I'm from,
they're monsters that appear sometimes.

06:52.370 --> 06:55.498
[Laios] <i>On days when the fog is thick
or there's a heavy snowstorm,</i>

06:55.582 --> 06:58.501
<i>walk through the hills
and you'll suddenly have extra companions.</i>

06:58.585 --> 07:01.004
That's when the Shapeshifter
copies your appearance

07:01.087 --> 07:03.006
and blends themselves
with the rest of your group.

07:03.089 --> 07:05.467
Wherever you're from… sounds scary.

07:05.550 --> 07:07.135
[Marcille A] Is it some type of fairy?

07:07.218 --> 07:08.845
[Chilchuck A]
Are they prone to causing trouble?

07:08.928 --> 07:10.180
If they go unnoticed,

07:10.263 --> 07:12.223
they'll kill and eat the real one
and take their place.

07:12.307 --> 07:13.266
-What the hell?
-Huh?

07:13.349 --> 07:15.059
-We have to hurry and find the fake ones!
-[panicked groan]

07:15.143 --> 07:15.977
-Huh?
-[scared breath]

07:16.060 --> 07:17.228
[panicked exclaim]

07:17.312 --> 07:18.730
I must eat.

07:18.813 --> 07:20.482
Well, this isn't good.

07:20.565 --> 07:23.067
Hey, those Laioses over there…

07:23.151 --> 07:25.487
I think it's pretty safe
to say they're fake.

07:25.570 --> 07:26.988
[Senshi A] Sounds about right.

07:27.071 --> 07:29.991
Yeah, they don't look like
they know much about monsters.

07:30.074 --> 07:32.869
Shapeshifters will read
the minds of living creatures,

07:32.952 --> 07:35.580
mimicking the appearance
of those around them.

07:35.663 --> 07:37.457
So the three other me's over there

07:37.540 --> 07:40.960
reflect how the real Senshi, Marcille,
and Chilchuck remember me.

07:41.461 --> 07:43.004
That makes sense.

07:43.087 --> 07:44.380
[Marcille A] If you look closely,

07:44.464 --> 07:47.425
you can see each version looks
somewhat different than the rest.

07:48.468 --> 07:50.720
[Marcille B] Can we hurry
and do something about this one then?

07:50.803 --> 07:51.638
Huh?

07:51.721 --> 07:53.640
[Marcille B] She's clearly a fake.

07:53.723 --> 07:54.599
Sure is.

07:54.682 --> 07:55.850
How dare you!

07:55.934 --> 07:57.644
Gaze upon my visage and see that I am…

07:57.727 --> 07:59.312
Ugh, so annoying.

07:59.395 --> 08:01.022
Whose memory did she come from?

08:01.105 --> 08:03.399
This Senshi and Chilchuck
are clearly fakes as well.

08:03.483 --> 08:04.317
[both] Hmm?

08:04.400 --> 08:05.318
How so?

08:05.401 --> 08:07.487
-[Chilchuck C and Chilchuck D] Huh?
-[Chilchuck C] Just look at him!

08:07.570 --> 08:10.031
My neck wrap isn't a scarf, but his is.

08:10.114 --> 08:12.158
[Chilchuck A]
And Senshi's helmet's missing holes.

08:12.242 --> 08:13.326
[soft grunt]

08:13.910 --> 08:15.662
Now that you mention it…

08:15.745 --> 08:17.247
[Chilchuck A]
I don't think there's any doubt

08:17.330 --> 08:19.290
that they're from Laios' memory.

08:19.374 --> 08:21.167
[Senshi A] He's not great with details.

08:21.251 --> 08:23.920
-[gate thuds]
-[fakes sobbing, grumbling]

08:24.003 --> 08:25.964
Is it fine to leave them like that?

08:26.047 --> 08:28.925
They don't really have
the same intelligence a human does.

08:29.008 --> 08:32.303
But if you do try to attack them,
they're sure to fight back.

08:32.845 --> 08:36.182
Let's avoid fighting unknown monsters
under these circumstances.

08:36.766 --> 08:39.852
We'll reveal the fakes peacefully
and then deal with them all!

08:39.936 --> 08:41.396
[gong strikes]

08:42.522 --> 08:44.399
His enthusiasm is great, but…

08:44.482 --> 08:46.234
Will he really be able
to tell the difference

08:46.317 --> 08:47.902
between the real one and the fakes?

08:47.986 --> 08:49.445
[Senshi A] Not likely.

08:49.529 --> 08:52.949
[Laios]
<i>The number of fakes remaining is six.</i>

08:53.533 --> 08:56.536
<i>When they're side by side,
you can see lots of differences.</i>

08:56.619 --> 09:00.373
<i>But while we're figuring this out,
our fuzzy memories are being influenced.</i>

09:00.456 --> 09:02.959
<i>I need to hurry and settle this or else…</i>

09:03.042 --> 09:06.170
[Senshi A] When it comes to the Marcilles,
they have different hairstyles.

09:06.254 --> 09:08.339
I honestly don't remember
what her hair looked like

09:08.423 --> 09:10.341
-when I last saw her.
-[Marcilles] You're kidding?

09:10.425 --> 09:13.094
This hairstyle's unique,
so you remember it, don't you?

09:13.177 --> 09:14.012
Just look at it!

09:14.095 --> 09:16.472
The blizzard made me cold,
so I took my hair down.

09:16.556 --> 09:19.183
First of all,
my hair quality is way better.

09:19.267 --> 09:21.603
Hair is a magic-user's life, you know?

09:21.686 --> 09:24.272
They're all saying
things the real one would say.

09:24.355 --> 09:27.692
Well, they are acting
the way we see Marcille in our heads.

09:28.276 --> 09:29.527
[all sigh]

09:30.194 --> 09:31.863
Oh! Here's an idea!

09:31.946 --> 09:35.366
How about we decide based on information
that only I would know?

09:35.450 --> 09:38.161
I hope you don't mean stuff
like guessing your mom's maiden name.

09:38.244 --> 09:40.246
-[Marcille A] Not that.
-[rustling]

09:40.955 --> 09:42.540
[Marcille A] Look at my spellbook!

09:43.583 --> 09:45.043
-[worried gasp]
-You see?

09:45.126 --> 09:46.044
[boys exclaim]

09:46.127 --> 09:48.546
Yeah, one of those books
is obviously fake.

09:49.088 --> 09:51.924
Hard to tell with the other two,
they both look legitimate.

09:52.008 --> 09:53.259
[Marcille B] What? No way!

09:53.343 --> 09:55.094
The spells in her book are all messed up!

09:55.178 --> 09:56.512
Hey, that's my line!

09:56.596 --> 09:57.889
[both grunt angrily]

09:57.972 --> 10:00.892
Our personal belongings
might help reveal more fakes.

10:00.975 --> 10:03.269
-Senshi, mind showing your stuff?
-Mm.

10:07.857 --> 10:09.567
Lock 'em up with the others!

10:10.360 --> 10:13.279
-[gate thuds]
-[sad groaning]

10:14.113 --> 10:16.824
[Laios]
<i>We've narrowed it down to two each, but…</i>

10:17.367 --> 10:19.035
<i>we're at a standstill.</i>

10:19.118 --> 10:22.997
<i>The number of fakes remaining… three.</i>

10:25.458 --> 10:27.543
Okay. Let's make food.

10:27.627 --> 10:29.420
[all] Wait, at a time like this?

10:29.504 --> 10:32.090
I can't tell you apart based on looks.

10:32.173 --> 10:35.176
So now,
I've got to check for usual behavior.

10:35.259 --> 10:38.930
I'll have all of you cook
and observe how you do things.

10:39.013 --> 10:41.432
That will tell me
which are fake and which are real.

10:43.518 --> 10:46.270
[Marcille A] <i>He didn't know
he encountered the mad mage</i>

10:46.354 --> 10:48.189
<i>or notice Shuro's feelings…</i>

10:48.272 --> 10:49.607
[Chilchuck A]
<i>He didn't pick up on the fact</i>

10:49.691 --> 10:52.068
<i>that he'd already met
that Kabru guy either.</i>

10:52.151 --> 10:55.196
[Senshi A] <i>And we're gonna rely
on his observational skills?</i>

10:55.279 --> 10:57.740
[silence]

10:57.824 --> 10:59.992
[Laios' party] This is bad.

11:00.743 --> 11:03.705
[Laios] <i>Who are my party members
and who are the imposters?</i>

11:03.788 --> 11:06.374
<i>It's my chance
to regain the trust that I lost.</i>

11:06.457 --> 11:08.501
<i>I really don't want
to disappoint them again.</i>

11:09.085 --> 11:12.130
<i>I have to pick up
on the subtle differences no matter what!</i>

11:12.713 --> 11:14.257
[Senshi A] We're dealing with Laios.

11:14.340 --> 11:16.926
There's a possibility
he might find the fakes more interesting

11:17.009 --> 11:18.678
because they're monsters.

11:18.761 --> 11:20.263
[Marcille A and Chilchuck A] That's true.

11:20.346 --> 11:22.974
[Laios' party] <i>We have to do
something about this ourselves!</i>

11:23.724 --> 11:25.518
I'll be watching from here.

11:25.601 --> 11:27.019
So do your best, everyone.

11:27.103 --> 11:28.312
Jeez, thanks.

11:28.396 --> 11:29.647
What should we make?

11:29.730 --> 11:32.233
[Senshi A]
<i>There's what I found on the fifth floor</i>

11:32.316 --> 11:35.695
<i>and the ingredients
Maizuru was kind enough to give to us.</i>

11:36.237 --> 11:40.408
<i>With such good provisions on our hands,
I've got an idea of what to make.</i>

11:40.491 --> 11:41.993
Before you all start…

11:42.076 --> 11:45.913
pair up with your other self
and work as a team to prepare a dish.

11:45.997 --> 11:47.165
[all] Huh?

11:47.248 --> 11:51.294
By having you perform the same assignment,
I can watch for different behaviors.

11:51.878 --> 11:53.588
[Laios] Senshi can teach you the recipe.

11:54.130 --> 11:55.673
Now, that's settled,

11:55.756 --> 11:57.425
is everyone ready?

11:57.508 --> 11:59.260
-[gong strikes]
-Let the cooking begin!

12:01.012 --> 12:03.181
[Laios] <i>First, the Chilchuck team.</i>

12:03.764 --> 12:04.807
<i>Cut the meat.</i>

12:04.891 --> 12:07.435
<i>And then mix the eggs and seasonings.</i>

12:07.518 --> 12:09.562
<i>Chilchuck A sat in the hallway,</i>

12:09.645 --> 12:13.483
<i>Chilchuck B sat on top of a wooden box
and started prepping.</i>

12:13.566 --> 12:14.817
What are you even writing?

12:14.901 --> 12:16.194
You're distracting!

12:16.277 --> 12:18.196
[Chilchuck B grunting]

12:19.280 --> 12:20.448
-[grunting continues]
-Hmm?

12:20.531 --> 12:22.783
It won't budge. Can you get it, Laios?

12:22.867 --> 12:23.701
Huh?

12:23.784 --> 12:25.286
Hey! You see that?

12:25.369 --> 12:27.288
B slipped up! He's the fake one!

12:27.371 --> 12:29.207
[Marcille A]
Huh? What are you talking about?

12:29.290 --> 12:31.292
[Chilchuck A] Oh, come on!
You guys know me!

12:31.375 --> 12:33.878
I've got lots of conviction
and pride and all that.

12:33.961 --> 12:36.839
[Senshi A] It's important
that people help each other, Chilchuck.

12:36.923 --> 12:39.008
[Marcille A] A is a little cynical,
don't you think?

12:39.091 --> 12:42.178
[Senshi A] If you look closely,
he's got some mean-looking eyes.

12:42.261 --> 12:43.346
Hey.

12:43.429 --> 12:45.515
-Our Chilchuck is definitely much cuter.
-[Chilchuck B grunting]

12:45.598 --> 12:46.724
Leave me alone!

12:46.807 --> 12:49.852
Hey, Laios,
you know I'm the real one, right?

12:50.520 --> 12:52.104
[Laios] <i>Chilchuck A…</i>

12:52.188 --> 12:55.483
<i>He does have
a pretty suspicious-looking face.</i>

12:55.566 --> 12:57.109
-<i>He might be the fake.</i>
-[nervous groan]

12:57.193 --> 12:58.361
We'll see.

12:58.444 --> 13:00.112
Please continue cooking.

13:01.197 --> 13:02.323
Dumbass.

13:02.823 --> 13:05.117
Insulted me in the common language.

13:05.826 --> 13:07.870
[Laios] <i>Next, the Marcille team.</i>

13:07.954 --> 13:10.748
I'm sorry,
but what is this egg that we're using?

13:10.831 --> 13:12.124
[Senshi A] It's a Harpy egg.

13:12.208 --> 13:13.501
[angry groan]

13:13.584 --> 13:15.670
I've said this
plenty of times since the start

13:15.753 --> 13:17.505
that humanoid monsters are off-limits!

13:17.588 --> 13:20.883
Yes, I've started to compromise,
but it's still not okay!

13:21.467 --> 13:25.054
[Laios] <i>Marcille B is behaving normally,
but maybe to a fault.</i>

13:25.137 --> 13:26.138
<i>Back to the recipe…</i>

13:26.764 --> 13:28.891
<i>Boil the diced Dryads.</i>

13:29.475 --> 13:31.269
What do you think, Marcille A?

13:31.352 --> 13:33.020
I don't like it, but…

13:33.604 --> 13:36.190
I've already eaten
fish-man eggs and Dryads,

13:36.274 --> 13:38.359
so why bother complaining now?

13:38.442 --> 13:41.779
If it meant that I could save Falin,
then I'd do anything.

13:41.862 --> 13:42.738
[all exclaim]

13:42.822 --> 13:44.240
Hey! I…

13:44.323 --> 13:47.118
I would also do anything
to save Falin, you know!

13:47.201 --> 13:49.328
B's determination is weak in comparison.

13:49.412 --> 13:52.290
Do I have to eat these Harpy eggs
to make you believe me?

13:52.957 --> 13:55.293
[Laios] <i>When the eggs are soft enough
to pierce with a chopstick,</i>

13:55.376 --> 13:56.294
<i>drain the water,</i>

13:56.377 --> 13:58.796
<i>mix with the seasonings and mash.</i>

13:59.380 --> 14:01.632
<i>Wait, this is actually tough.</i>

14:01.716 --> 14:04.135
<i>They both said things
the real one would say.</i>

14:04.218 --> 14:05.803
<i>Back to the Senshi team.</i>

14:06.387 --> 14:09.098
So, where did you get
those Harpy eggs from anyway?

14:09.181 --> 14:12.268
[Senshi B] I came across a nest
inside of a collapsed house,

14:12.351 --> 14:14.562
so I gathered everything that was there.

14:15.187 --> 14:17.023
[Laios] <i>Cut to one-centimeter thick.</i>

14:17.648 --> 14:20.610
As they say, eggs are the perfect…

14:20.693 --> 14:21.944
Source of nutrients.

14:22.028 --> 14:23.446
[both chuckle]

14:24.030 --> 14:26.949
[Laios]
<i>Fry with rice on low heat and then season.</i>

14:27.033 --> 14:30.202
I'm pretty sure
rice is Shuro's favorite food.

14:30.286 --> 14:32.496
[Senshi A] It's packed
with plenty of essential nutrients

14:32.580 --> 14:34.582
adventurers need to explore.

14:34.665 --> 14:36.959
We're real lucky to find
as much as we did.

14:37.543 --> 14:39.754
[Laios] <i>I'm only interested
in eating monsters we find,</i>

14:39.837 --> 14:41.422
<i>but Senshi's different.</i>

14:41.505 --> 14:43.507
<i>He's focused on deeper things.</i>

14:43.591 --> 14:46.594
<i>Like taking flavor and nutrition
into account.</i>

14:46.677 --> 14:48.763
<i>All the food looks so good.</i>

14:48.846 --> 14:50.932
-<i>Guess I can't decide based on skill.</i>
-[exclaims]

14:51.015 --> 14:52.516
[Marcille B] Hmm…

14:52.600 --> 14:55.144
You know,
no one's really said anything about it,

14:55.227 --> 14:56.604
so I thought I'd check.

14:57.188 --> 14:58.606
[Marcille B] But doesn't Senshi B

14:58.689 --> 15:01.108
looked a little more attractive
than he should?

15:01.734 --> 15:03.110
[dramatic gasps]

15:05.696 --> 15:07.114
Seems fine to me.

15:07.198 --> 15:09.033
Yeah, Senshi's always looked handsome.

15:09.116 --> 15:10.117
[Marcille B and Senshi A] Huh?

15:10.201 --> 15:12.787
What even is this?
Prejudice against dwarves?

15:12.870 --> 15:15.373
Yeah, come on.
Senshi doesn't look that dopey.

15:15.456 --> 15:17.792
-[panicked groaning]
-[Laios] <i>Senshi is handsome.</i>

15:17.875 --> 15:19.126
<i>Noted.</i>

15:22.254 --> 15:24.006
[Senshi B] Laios, the food's almost ready.

15:24.090 --> 15:26.258
Have you made your final decision yet?

15:26.842 --> 15:28.010
[Laios] <i>Honestly…</i>

15:28.094 --> 15:29.720
-[warbling]
-<i>…I have no idea.</i>

15:29.804 --> 15:32.848
<i>They all look like
they could be real… or fake.</i>

15:32.932 --> 15:35.101
<i>Besides, I think
it's kind of unfair to have me</i>

15:35.184 --> 15:38.521
<i>try to distinguish a memory in my head
against the actual thing.</i>

15:39.146 --> 15:42.316
<i>It would've been fun to look
for a monster disguised as a human,</i>

15:42.400 --> 15:44.402
<i>but trying to see through an illusion is…</i>

15:46.487 --> 15:48.948
<i>Look for a monster, huh?</i>

15:49.031 --> 15:51.033
-[Senshi A] It's ready!
-Hmm?

15:51.117 --> 15:52.410
MEMORIES OF THE FIFTH FLOOR PILAF

15:52.493 --> 15:53.327
SWEET DRYAD

15:53.411 --> 15:54.537
THE WHOLE FIFTH FLOOR PICCATA

15:54.620 --> 15:56.872
All right, listen up while you eat.

15:57.373 --> 15:59.625
Those of you I think are real are…

16:00.126 --> 16:01.794
Chilchuck A!

16:02.378 --> 16:04.171
[Laios] <i>The one with the dour expression!</i>

16:04.797 --> 16:06.424
[Laios] Marcille B!

16:06.507 --> 16:09.301
<i>The one who won't eat Harpy eggs
even if it's for Falin.</i>

16:09.927 --> 16:11.012
Senshi A!

16:11.095 --> 16:12.304
<i>The dopey one!</i>

16:12.888 --> 16:13.889
That said,

16:13.973 --> 16:16.350
will the imposters
promptly lock themselves in the cell?

16:16.434 --> 16:18.060
[Marcilles and Chilchucks]
Now hold on a second!

16:18.144 --> 16:20.354
What kind of proof do you have
that he's the real one?

16:21.022 --> 16:22.690
That one's obviously the imposter!

16:23.315 --> 16:25.067
What makes you think she's real?

16:25.151 --> 16:26.110
Hmm…

16:26.193 --> 16:27.319
Just a feeling.

16:27.987 --> 16:29.780
I'll try to explain all of that later.

16:30.322 --> 16:32.199
Let's deal with the fake ones first.

16:32.283 --> 16:33.743
It's…

16:33.826 --> 16:35.327
Just a feeling?

16:35.911 --> 16:36.871
"Deal with"?

16:36.954 --> 16:39.081
I knew it, this guy's a joke.

16:39.165 --> 16:41.042
[Senshi B] It seems like…

16:41.125 --> 16:43.586
[Senshi A] We're just gonna
have to protect ourselves.

16:43.669 --> 16:44.754
-[muffled groan]
-[Chilchuck A grunts]

16:45.755 --> 16:46.922
[Laios' party grunting]

16:47.006 --> 16:49.925
[Laios] <i>This was inevitable
no matter who I picked.</i>

16:50.009 --> 16:53.345
<i>Shapeshifter is a term
for monsters that mimic others.</i>

16:54.013 --> 16:56.682
<i>There are kinds
that can mimic voices or possess</i>

16:56.766 --> 16:58.476
<i>or physically change their appearance.</i>

16:59.143 --> 17:01.437
<i>Which is this Shapeshifter capable of?</i>

17:02.146 --> 17:05.149
<i>There's no way
that monsters are able to cook food.</i>

17:05.232 --> 17:07.943
<i>It must be creating an illusion
like Marcille said.</i>

17:08.652 --> 17:12.573
<i>Since it targets people,
it's either a carnivore or an omnivore.</i>

17:12.656 --> 17:15.951
<i>It's too much of a coward
and lacks the strength to attack directly.</i>

17:16.702 --> 17:19.455
<i>Visibility is low and it's cold here.</i>

17:19.538 --> 17:23.459
<i>So it can withstand the cold
and relies on smell and hearing.</i>

17:24.460 --> 17:25.586
Hmm…

17:26.128 --> 17:28.089
<i>Downwind is that direction.</i>

17:28.672 --> 17:31.592
<i>The enemy is waiting for us
to wear ourselves out.</i>

17:31.675 --> 17:34.970
<i>I doubt I'll hit it
by recklessly swinging my sword around.</i>

17:35.554 --> 17:37.348
<i>So what should I do?</i>

17:37.431 --> 17:39.809
<i>Kensuke's gotten pretty quiet.</i>

17:39.892 --> 17:41.477
<i>He might die from the cold.</i>

17:42.686 --> 17:45.189
<i>Guess I'll have to take a page
from the enemy.</i>

17:45.272 --> 17:49.360
<i>Time to turn the tables
and make the hunter… feel like the hunted.</i>

17:49.443 --> 17:52.613
<i>It's been a while, but I'll do</i> that.

17:52.696 --> 17:55.616
[Laios' party grunting]

17:57.451 --> 17:58.994
[determined grunt]

17:59.078 --> 18:01.163
[tense music playing]

18:02.081 --> 18:03.290
[inhales deeply]

18:03.374 --> 18:04.250
[music stops]

18:06.210 --> 18:07.461
[barks]

18:07.545 --> 18:09.130
[all gasp]

18:09.213 --> 18:11.715
-[Laios barking]
-[dramatic music playing]

18:14.218 --> 18:15.594
[Senshi A] A dog?

18:15.678 --> 18:16.637
Whoa!

18:16.720 --> 18:18.389
[Senshi A] Wait, a hunting dog?

18:18.472 --> 18:22.143
[Laios] <i>For as long as I can remember,
dogs have always been by my side,</i>

18:22.226 --> 18:23.894
<i>and I've learned a lot from them.</i>

18:24.395 --> 18:25.646
<i>How to hunt,</i>

18:25.729 --> 18:28.482
<i>how to engage
with a threat stronger than you are.</i>

18:28.566 --> 18:30.359
-<i>And now, let me teach you!</i>
-[dogs barking]

18:30.442 --> 18:31.819
-[growls]
-[dogs howling]

18:31.902 --> 18:33.070
He's good!

18:33.154 --> 18:34.488
[Senshi A] Laios really is…

18:34.572 --> 18:35.656
A dog!

18:35.739 --> 18:37.575
[Laios] <i>You may think you're the hunter,</i>

18:37.658 --> 18:39.994
<i>but you're actually the one being hunted!</i>

18:40.911 --> 18:41.871
[gasps]

18:41.954 --> 18:44.915
Everyone, look! The illusions!

18:44.999 --> 18:46.250
-[Senshi] Huh?
-[exclaims]

18:47.293 --> 18:48.210
[Chilchuck] Huh?

18:53.174 --> 18:55.217
[epic music playing]

18:57.511 --> 19:00.181
[Laios] <i>So, you've finally shown yourself.</i>

19:00.264 --> 19:03.184
<i>Since you're a beast,
you should know full well.</i>

19:03.267 --> 19:04.560
<i>In this fight…</i>

19:06.020 --> 19:09.982
<i>the one who flinches first
is the one who loses!</i>

19:10.065 --> 19:10.941
[growls]

19:11.025 --> 19:14.028
[both shout]
Laios! No!

19:14.778 --> 19:17.114
[music swells]

19:20.201 --> 19:21.118
[music stops]

19:21.202 --> 19:23.621
[loud blast]

19:23.704 --> 19:25.289
[Laios groans]

19:29.668 --> 19:32.171
[frizzling]

19:34.298 --> 19:35.299
[blows air]

19:37.343 --> 19:38.969
[Chilchuck] You all right, Laios?

19:39.053 --> 19:40.638
All right in the head, that is?

19:41.222 --> 19:42.348
Uh-huh.

19:42.431 --> 19:44.266
[Chilchuck]
There's a lot of things I wanna say,

19:44.350 --> 19:46.393
but how come you didn't draw your weapon?

19:46.477 --> 19:48.854
[Laios]
Honestly, I got too into character.

19:48.938 --> 19:50.356
-[Senshi exclaims]
-[Chilchuck] Hmm?

19:52.316 --> 19:54.860
[Senshi] Look what happened
to all the food we made.

19:54.944 --> 19:57.404
Makes sense
since we cooked it with an illusion.

19:57.488 --> 19:58.822
[Chilchuck] Let's remake it.

20:00.282 --> 20:01.325
[Chilchuck] Man,

20:01.408 --> 20:04.536
hard to believe that Laios' intuition
was actually on the nose.

20:04.620 --> 20:06.497
[Marcille] So, how did you tell us apart?

20:06.580 --> 20:07.456
Hmm…

20:07.539 --> 20:09.500
By the lack of monster awareness?

20:10.084 --> 20:11.126
[all] Hmm?

20:11.710 --> 20:14.463
[Laios] <i>Well, first,
Chilchuck sat on a wooden box.</i>

20:14.546 --> 20:18.050
<i>Boxes are the perfect hiding spot
for Mimics and Tentacles.</i>

20:18.133 --> 20:21.387
<i>For you to not even worry about that
kinda stuck out to me.</i>

20:21.470 --> 20:24.682
[Senshi B] I came across a nest
inside of a collapsed house,

20:24.765 --> 20:27.017
so I gathered everything that was there.

20:27.601 --> 20:30.104
[Laios] <i>For someone who respects
the balance of an ecosystem,</i>

20:30.187 --> 20:32.022
<i>that seemed a bit careless.</i>

20:32.106 --> 20:35.025
Do I have to eat these Harpy eggs
to make you believe me?

20:35.901 --> 20:38.529
[Laios] <i>Lastly, when Marcille dumped
the boiling water.</i>

20:38.612 --> 20:40.614
<i>After how you were attacked
by that Undine,</i>

20:40.698 --> 20:42.992
<i>doing something like that seemed reckless.</i>

20:43.075 --> 20:44.910
<i>That's why it caught my attention.</i>

20:45.703 --> 20:47.746
[soft grunt]
Huh?

20:49.164 --> 20:50.541
[shocked gasp]

20:50.624 --> 20:55.004
In this case, it was that absentmindedness
that made me think you were the real one.

20:55.087 --> 20:56.422
Huh.

20:56.505 --> 20:58.173
[Senshi] That was some good work.

20:58.257 --> 21:00.467
I'm real proud of you, Laios.

21:00.551 --> 21:03.304
I think
his perspective is still a bit off.

21:03.387 --> 21:04.972
Well… still,

21:05.055 --> 21:07.933
it's not easy
to see through an illusion spell.

21:08.017 --> 21:10.811
It did keep the Shapeshifter fed
after all.

21:11.395 --> 21:12.938
I thought you noticed then…

21:13.022 --> 21:15.607
I've already eaten
fish-man eggs and Dryads.

21:16.275 --> 21:19.361
[Marcille] <i>When she mentioned
the fish-man eggs in particular…</i>

21:19.445 --> 21:20.946
It should have been obvious.

21:21.030 --> 21:23.615
I mean, we've never eaten
those kinds of eggs before.

21:23.699 --> 21:24.616
Right, guys?

21:25.951 --> 21:27.286
[Marcille giggles]

21:27.369 --> 21:28.537
-[exclaims]
-[Chilchuck grunts]

21:29.288 --> 21:31.373
[Marcille]
<i>Could it have been that barley dish?</i>

21:33.834 --> 21:35.669
[Senshi] The dessert's ready now too.

21:35.753 --> 21:37.004
-[Laios and Chilchuck] All right!
-[Marcille] Yippee!

21:37.087 --> 21:39.423
It's been a while since we've had sweets.

21:39.506 --> 21:41.008
[Senshi] Should I make some tea?

21:41.592 --> 21:44.803
Pretty sure there were tea leaves
in the bag of provisions we got.

21:44.887 --> 21:46.013
Hmm?

21:46.096 --> 21:47.973
Did you put it somewhere else?

21:48.057 --> 21:50.851
[Senshi]
No, I definitely put it right here.

21:50.934 --> 21:51.769
Hmm?

21:55.064 --> 21:56.357
[Chilchuck] <i>The rice…</i>

21:58.359 --> 21:59.777
[Marcille] Huh?

21:59.860 --> 22:02.154
[uneasy music playing]

22:10.120 --> 22:11.121
[gasps]

22:12.247 --> 22:13.624
[Chilchuck] Empty.

22:15.125 --> 22:16.752
-[Marcille screams]
-[gasps]

22:17.336 --> 22:18.754
[scared gasp]

22:18.837 --> 22:20.506
[Laios] Marcille!

22:21.256 --> 22:23.383
[Asebi] Drop your weapon and freeze.

22:23.467 --> 22:25.969
Do that and we can talk peacefully.

22:28.347 --> 22:29.598
[tense sting]

22:31.058 --> 22:33.352
[closing theme music playing]
